---
source: crates/lighthouse-cli/tests/it/surface.rs
expression: "printed(dir.path(), &args)"
---
Entry points for agent hooks. Reads the hook payload on stdin.

For Claude Code, see docs/agents.md.

Usage: lighthouse hook [OPTIONS] <AGENT> <EVENT>

Arguments:
  <AGENT>
          [possible values: claude-code]

  <EVENT>
          Possible values:
          - pre-tool-use:  Before Edit, Write or MultiEdit: record the file's findings as the session's baseline, once per file; prints nothing
          - post-tool-use: After Edit, Write or MultiEdit: report the findings the edit introduced
          - stop:          When the agent wants to stop: report the findings the session introduced

Options:
      --allow-incomplete
          Say that the analysis was incomplete but do not block on it

      --config <FILE>
          The project file; the project root is then the current directory
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_CONFIG=]

      --color <COLOR>
          Color of help and messages. `auto` honours NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE
          
          [env: LIGHTHOUSE_COLOR=]
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
